  <Docs>
    <summary>Callback interface for NFC-related events.</summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>Callback interface for NFC-related events.
            
            These callbacks will be called when registered with
            <c>#registerNfcEventCallback(Executor, NfcEventCallback)</c> and while the registered caller
            is still alive. When you are done listening to the callbacks, you should unregister it with
            <c>#unregisterNfcEventCallback(NfcEventCallback)</c>.</para>
      <para>
        <format type="text/html">
          <a href="https://developer.android.com/reference/android/nfc/cardemulation/CardEmulation.NfcEventCallback" title="Reference documentation">Java documentation for <code>android.nfc.cardemulation.CardEmulation.NfcEventCallback</code>.</a>
        </format>
      </para>
